# docs/ is the GitHub Pages root (main:/docs). Only the data files index.html
# and methods.html actually fetch are committed; everything else the exporters
# in scripts/site_export/ write stays local. Owner, 2026-10-19: "keep the data
# off of the repo".
#
# Ignore the whole data tree, then re-include the committed keep-list below.
# Re-deriving the list: grep -oE '(data/)[A-Za-z0-9_/.-]+' index.html methods.html
data/*

# loaded by index.html on first paint
!data/bayarea_counties.json
!data/bodies.json
!data/meetings.json
!data/episodes.json
!data/terms.json
!data/panels.json
!data/nimby_points.json
!data/panels/
# data/figs/ holds the topic-time and pilot role-gap figures. No page fetches them
# since the topic-time panel came off index.html on 2026-10-20, but they are kept in
# the repo: REPORT.md cites them by filename.
!data/figs/
# data/models/summary.json is NOT re-included: index.html stopped fetching it with
# that panel, and export_site_data.py no longer writes it, so a committed copy could
# only go stale. The figures and posterior tables it indexed are still copied.

# loaded by methods.html
!data/flow.json
!data/methods.json

# index.html hard-codes LEAD_EPISODE = "gr-fremont-21_e4" and loads that body's
# turns on first paint, so this one shard (0.43 MB) is part of the landing view.
# Without it the published page logs a 404 before anyone clicks anything.
!data/episodes/
data/episodes/*
!data/episodes/fremont.json

# Deliberately NOT committed:
#   data/episodes/*     the other 26 bodies' full meeting turns, 18.4 MB,
#                       fetched only when a reader opens that body. They 404 on
#                       the published site; loadText() catches it and shows an
#                       empty text pane. See README.md "Dashboard".
#   data/bodies_geo.csv an INPUT to export_site_data.py and
#                       export_nimby_points.py, not loaded by any page. Keep a
#                       local copy or the exporters cannot run.
#   data/site_numbers.json  written by export_panels.py, read by no page today.
#   data/tables/        copied from output/analysis/models/, read by no page today.

# local screenshot runs
screenshots/
